## Retrieval Definitions

Surface

A recruiter-visible phrase.

Association

A retrieval-only phrase.

Hit

An Aho-Corasick phrase match.

Coverage

Percentage of job descriptions
containing at least one phrase.

Density

Hits per job description.

Frequency

Phrase occurrence count
across corpus.

Freeze Spot

Phrase with zero observed hits.

Dead Phrase

Phrase with hit rate below threshold.


## Coverage Density Rule

recruiter_surfaces should maximize market vocabulary coverage for the capability.

Each anchor should contain multiple recruiter-recognizable capability expressions where they represent legitimate market wording.

The goal is lexical coverage, not synonym inflation.

Example:

Good:

workflow orchestration
workflow engine
business process automation
stateful workflow

Bad:

workflow orchestration
workflow orchestration implementation
workflow orchestration experience
workflow orchestration knowledge

These are template variants, not capability variants.


## Canonical Surface Quality

recruiter_surfaces must function as canonical capability vocabulary.

Every recruiter_surface must:

- be recruiter recognizable
- be ATS searchable
- be capability oriented
- be vendor neutral
- be reusable across multiple templates
- remain meaningful outside template expansion

A recruiter_surface must not depend on surrounding template text to become understandable.


## Recruiter Surface Ownership Rule

recruiter_surfaces represent canonical
market capability vocabulary.

recruiter_surfaces must not contain:

- responsibility wording
- requirement wording
- preference wording
- experience wording
- template-derived phrasing

Examples

Good:
workflow orchestration
workflow engine
business process automation

Bad:
experience with workflow orchestration
workflow orchestration experience
knowledge of workflow orchestration


## Retrieval Precision Validation

Every recruiter_surface must:

- be independently searchable
- be meaningful without template context
- be suitable for exact matching
- be suitable for Aho-Corasick indexing

Reject if:

- contains template wording
- contains experience wording
- contains responsibility wording
- contains requirement wording

Examples:

Good:

workflow orchestration
service integration
event processing

Bad:

experience with workflow orchestration
hands-on workflow orchestration
knowledge of event processing


## Aho-Corasick Retrieval Validation

Every recruiter_surface must:

- be meaningful standalone
- appear plausibly as exact JD text
- maximize lexical retrieval density
- avoid template wording
- avoid role wording
- avoid sentence fragments

Reject:

understanding of workflow orchestration
experience with workflow orchestration

Accept:

workflow orchestration
workflow engine
business process automation

===

Coverage quality is measured by
discriminative retrieval coverage,
not vocabulary count.

Adding vocabulary that increases
false-positive rate decreases coverage quality.

## RetrievalOptimizationObjective

Coverage optimization shall maximize

Precision × Recall

subject to:

- anchor semantics preserved
- abstraction boundaries preserved
- false-positive rate bounded
- deterministic retrieval maintained

Generation must not optimize solely for:

- maximum vocabulary size
- minimum vocabulary size

Vocabulary quality is preferred over vocabulary quantity.

## NodeDiscriminativeCoverageRule

retrieval_associations should collectively provide
independent retrieval evidence.

Preferred dimensions include:

- framework ecosystem
- runtime
- protocol
- deployment
- architecture
- common companion libraries

Avoid concentrating multiple associations on
the same lexical concept.

Coverage quality is measured by
discriminative diversity,
not vocabulary count.Metadata: relations.definition.rule.txt

## Relations Rule

Purpose

Relations are the source layer for recruiter-facing expansion.

They do not store final resume text.
They store the data needed to generate recruiter language and ATS language.

## Relation contract

Each anchor relation node must contain only:

```ts
{
  adjacent: AnchorId[];
  recruiter_surfaces: {
    vi: string[];
    en: string[];
  };
  retrieval_associations: string[];
}


## Field definitions
### adjacent

Anchor-to-anchor relations only.

Rules:

anchor ↔ anchor only
same abstraction level
recruiter co-occurrence
not a synonym list
not a vendor list

Good:

workflow_orchestration ↔ event_processing
background_job_processing ↔ message_queue_processing

Bad:

workflow_orchestration ↔ Temporal
workflow_orchestration ↔ docker
workflow_orchestration ↔ workflow_orchestration
recruiter_surfaces

### recruiter_surfaces, recruiter-visible capability language that may appear in:

JD requirements
JD responsibilities
recruiter searches
LinkedIn searches

Required shape:

vi: string[]
en: string[]

Rules:

Must be capability language
Must be vendor-neutral
Must survive vendor replacementterminology
Must sound like actual JD language
Must be recruiter-searchable
Good recruiter surfaces

For workflow_orchestration:

workflow engine
workflow orchestration
business process automation
state machine
event-driven workflow
Bad recruiter surfaces
Temporal workflow
MongoDB change stream
BullMQ worker
Jobs Watcher


## retrieval_associations

Recruiter-observed retrieval vocabulary related to the anchor.

Purpose:

- improve ATS retrieval coverage
- improve recruiter search coverage
- support template generation
- support retrieval expansion

May contain:

- technologies
- frameworks
- protocols
- patterns
- architectural terminology
- market terminology

Must:

- preserve anchor semantics
- remain recruiter-searchable
- remain ATS-searchable
- remain replaceable

Must not:

- become anchors
- introduce new capability meanings
- contain project names
- contain resume prose

## TECH/CAP/COMP/BEH anchors over profile.source.types.ts usage of relations.source.ts per RELATION NODE REQUIREMENTS

Every tech, cap, comp, beh anchor MUST contain:

- adjacent
- recruiter_surfaces.en
- recruiter_surfaces.vi
- retrieval_associations

Empty arrays are invalid.

The generator MUST NOT emit:

r([], [], [])

for any technology, competency, behavior, capability anchor.Metadata: relations.generation.rule.txt

## Purpose

Mandatory population requirements.

Every anchor defined in
profile.source.types.ts
must generate:

adjacent
recruiter_surfaces.en
recruiter_surfaces.vi
retrieval_associations

Empty arrays are invalid.

Generation requirements are owned by:
relations.generation.rule.txt

Coverage requirements are owned by:
relations.coverage.rule.txt

Validation requirements are owned by:
relations.validation.rule.txt

## ReplacementGenerationRule

When replacing retrieval_associations,
the generator shall preserve approximate lexical density.

Replacing low-quality associations with higher-quality
associations is preferred over deleting entries.

Large reductions in retrieval_association cardinality
require corpus-supported justification.Metadata: relations.population.rule.txt

## Purpose

Defines mandatory population rules for all
relation nodes.

Relations.source.ts may never emit empty
recruiter_surfaces or retrieval_associations
for any anchor defined in profile.source.types.ts.

## Rule:

### Capability anchor

CAP anchors generate:

recruiter_surfaces
    from recruiter language

retrieval_associations
    from ecosystem language


Example:

workflow_orchestration

must generate

recruiter_surfaces.en = [
 "workflow orchestration",
 "workflow engine",
 "business process automation",
 "workflow automation",
 "state machine workflow",
 ...
]

### Tech anchor 

TECH anchors MUST NOT be empty.

Technology anchors generate:

recruiter_surfaces
    from recruiter-facing usage language

retrieval_associations
    from ecosystem vocabulary


Example:

languageTech.go

must produce

recruiter_surfaces.en = [
 "golang development",
 "go backend development",
 "go microservices",
 "go services",
 "backend development with go",
 ...
]

and

retrieval_associations = [
 "Gin",
 "Fiber",
 "Echo",
 "Go modules",
 "gRPC",
 "PostgreSQL",
 "Docker",
 "Kubernetes",
 ...
]

### Surface derivation algorithm

For each anchor:

Generate recruiter_surfaces from:

1 canonical recruiter phrase
2 ATS phrase
3 LinkedIn recruiter phrase
4 hiring manager phrase
5 market phrase
6 Vietnam market phrase
7 abbreviation phrase
8 alternative JD phrase

until

lexical saturation


### Template compatibility validation

Every recruiter_surface MUST pass:

develop and maintain {surface}

experience with {surface}

knowledge of {surface}

Example:

Good

API development
workflow orchestration
service integration

Bad

experience with APIs
building APIs
API implementation experience

because templates will duplicate wording.

### Vendor template compatibility

Every retrieval_association must naturally fit:

experience with {retrieval_association}

working knowledge of {retrieval_association}

ability to integrate {retrieval_association}

Good:

Kafka
RabbitMQ
Temporal
PostgreSQL
Docker

Bad:

event processing
workflow orchestration
backend development

## DensityStabilityRule

Retrieval association density should remain relatively
stable across generations unless supported by corpus
evaluation.

Large reductions indicate possible recall regression
and require validation.Metadata: relations.template.rule.txt
RULE 1

recruiter_surfaces MUST produce natural recruiter language
when inserted into:

develop and maintain {surface}
experience with {surface}
knowledge of {surface}

RULE 2

retrieval_associations MUST produce natural ecosystem language
when inserted into:

experience with {retrieval_association}
working knowledge of {retrieval_association}
ability to integrate {retrieval_association}

RULE 3

If generated phrase sounds unnatural,
surface is invalid.Metadata: relations.validation.rule.txt

# RelationsValidationRule

## Purpose
This file defines the validation rules for `relations.source.ts` and its downstream use in `templates.source.ts`.

It is the enforcement layer for:
- bilingual recruiter surfaces
- retrieval associations
- adjacency correctness
- deterministic template generation
- replacement safety across markets

## Validation Contract

A relation node is valid only if all of the following hold:

- `adjacent` contains only anchor IDs.
- `recruiter_surfaces.vi` contains only Vietnamese recruiter-facing capability language.
- `recruiter_surfaces.en` contains only English recruiter-facing capability language.
- `retrieval_associations` contains recruiter-observed retrieval vocabulary
associated with the anchor.

It may contain:
- technologies
- frameworks
- protocols
- patterns
- architectural terminology
- market terminology

It must:
- improve retrieval coverage
- preserve anchor semantics
- remain replaceable
- remain recruiter-searchable
- remain ATS-searchable

It must not:
- introduce new anchor meanings
- contain project names
- contain resume prose
- contain role labels

- No field mixes capability, vendor, technology, project, or role layers.
- The node can generate deterministic template output without inventing new source data.

## Field Rules

### 1. `adjacent`
Must satisfy all of the following:

- anchor ↔ anchor only
- same abstraction level
- represents recruiter co-occurrence, not synonym expansion
- does not contain vendors, tools, or project names

Valid examples:
- `workflow_orchestration` ↔ `event_processing`
- `service_decomposition` ↔ `boundary_definition`

Invalid examples:
- `workflow_orchestration` ↔ `Temporal`
- `workflow_orchestration` ↔ `docker`
- `workflow_orchestration` ↔ `workflow_orchestration`

### 2. `recruiter_surfaces.vi`
Must satisfy all of the following:

- readable as real Vietnamese job-description language
- may include English technical terms commonly used in Vietnamese job posts
- must remain capability language
- must be vendor-neutral
- must survive vendor replacement
- must sound like something a recruiter would search or write
- recruiter-searchable
- ATS-searchable
- reusable across multiple template families
- meaningful outside templates
- lexical coverage increasing
- not merely a template variant

Good examples:
- `tích hợp hệ thống`
- `xử lý bất đồng bộ`
- `workflow orchestration`
- `thiết kế API`
- `mô hình hóa dữ liệu`

Bad examples:
- `điều phối quy trình công việc trạng thái hữu hạn`
- `MongoDB change stream`
- `Temporal workflow`
- `Jobs Watcher`

### 3. `recruiter_surfaces.en`
Must satisfy all of the following:

- readable as real English job-description language
- must be recruiter-searchable
- must remain capability language
- must be vendor-neutral
- must survive vendor replacement
- must map naturally to the anchor
- recruiter-searchable
- ATS-searchable
- reusable across multiple template families
- meaningful outside templates
- lexical coverage increasing
- not merely a template variant

Good examples:
- `workflow orchestration`
- `workflow engine`
- `business process automation`
- `service integration`
- `event processing`

Bad examples:
- `Temporal workflow`
- `MongoDB change stream`
- `backend engineer`
- `software development`

### 4. `retrieval_associations`
Must satisfy all of the following:

Must contain:
- recruiter-searchable vocabulary
- ATS-searchable vocabulary
- JD-observed vocabulary

May contain:
- technologies
- patterns
- architectural concepts

Must not:
- introduce new anchor meanings
- contain project names
- contain resume prose

Bad examples:
- project names
- role labels
- abstract capability names
- invented tools

## Retrieval Association Ownership Rule

retrieval_associations do not define anchor meaning.

Anchor meaning is owned exclusively by:

- profile.source.ts anchor
- recruiter_surfaces

Removing retrieval_associations must not change
the capability represented by the anchor.

## Bilingual Compliance Rules

### Rule B1
`recruiter_surfaces.vi` and `recruiter_surfaces.en` must be semantically aligned.

They may differ in surface form, but they must express the same capability.

Example:

```ts
recruiter_surfaces: {
  vi: ['tích hợp hệ thống', 'xử lý bất đồng bộ'],
  en: ['service integration', 'async processing']
}

### Rule B2

Neither language may introduce a new anchor meaning.

If the English surface says one capability and the Vietnamese surface says another, the node is invalid.

### Rule B3

Do not over-translate Vietnamese recruiter language.

Vietnamese recruiter language may keep English technical terms when those terms are standard in market usage.

Good:

workflow orchestration
workflow engine
message queue
event-driven
REST API

Bad:

điều phối quy trình công việc trạng thái hữu hạn
xử lý tuần tự hóa phân tán
Rule B4

Do not force literal symmetry between vi and en.

The correct goal is market-natural bilingual coverage, not word-for-word translation.


## Acceptance Rules

A relation node passes validation only if:

it stays within one abstraction layer
it supports bilingual recruiter language
it supports vendor replacement
it supports ATS exposure
it can generate templates deterministically
it remains backward-compatible with existing source shape

supports canonical recruiter vocabulary

supports template expansion

supports ATS retrieval vocabulary generation

supports vendor replacement

supports deterministic artifact generation

A relation node passes recruiter-surface validation only if:

1. recruiter_surfaces represent capability-level recruiter vocabulary

2. recruiter_surfaces are reusable across template families

3. recruiter_surfaces remain vendor-neutral

4. recruiter_surfaces improve ATS retrieval coverage

5. recruiter_surfaces can generate recruiter-natural responsibility templates

6. recruiter_surfaces can generate recruiter-natural requirement templates

7. recruiter_surfaces can generate recruiter-natural preference templates

## Rejection Rules

## Reject the node if any of the following is true:

it uses a tool as a recruiter surface
it uses a vendor as an anchor
it mixes capability and technology in one field
it contains non-market wording
it contains project-specific wording
it cannot generate stable bilingual templates
it breaks anchor ↔ relation ↔ template consistency

## Template Expandability

Every recruiter_surface must naturally fit responsibility, requirement, and preference templates.

Validation test:

experience with {surface}
knowledge of {surface}
develop and maintain {surface}

must produce recruiter-natural wording.

Example:

Good:

workflow orchestration
service integration
event processing

Bad:

good understanding of workflows
experience building APIs

because they already contain template semantics.


## Retrieval Density Validation

A capability relation node fails validation if:

recruiter_surfaces.en.length < 5

OR

recruiter_surfaces.vi.length < 5

OR

all recruiter_surfaces are lexical variants
of the same phrase.

Coverage must include distinct recruiter
retrieval phrases.

## Empty Vocabulary Rejection

Reject node if:

recruiter_surfaces.en is empty

OR

recruiter_surfaces.vi is empty

OR

retrieval_associations is empty
for capability anchors.

## RetrievalAssociationValidation

Reject if retrieval_associations contains:

- recruiter surface duplicates
- capability synonyms
- template wording
- responsibility wording
- requirement wording

Accept:

Kafka
RabbitMQ
NATS
Temporal
Camunda

Reject:

workflow orchestration
business process automation
service integration
event processing

FAIL IF

duplicate surfaces >20%

empty arrays

surface equals association

EN/VI mismatch

less than minimum lexical density

## Retrieval Association Specificity Rule
A retrieval_association is valid only if it provides
positive discrimination for the anchor.

Validation:

Compare occurrence frequency in:

A = job descriptions mentioning the anchor
B = job descriptions not mentioning the anchor

A retrieval_association is valid only if:

P(term | anchor) > P(term | non-anchor)

by a meaningful margin.

Examples:

Express.js

PASS:
middleware
express middleware
express router
npm

FAIL:
backend
api
performance
testing
software development

Example:

npm

appears in many jobs.

But:

P(npm | Express)
>>
P(npm | random backend JD)

So npm still has retrieval value.

## Retrieval Association Information Gain Rule

A retrieval_association must increase retrieval
information gain.

Removing the association should reduce
anchor-identification accuracy.

If removing the term causes no measurable
drop in retrieval quality,
the association is invalid.

Example:

Nuxt:

SSR
Vue
Nitro
hydration

Removing:

SSR

might hurt retrieval.

Valid.

Removing:

web development

Invalid.

## Corpus Frequency Rejection Rule

Reject retrieval_associations that occur
at high frequency across unrelated
software-engineering job descriptions.

A retrieval_association fails if:

global_corpus_frequency(term)
is significantly higher than
anchor_specific_frequency(term).

Examples:

FAIL:
backend
frontend
testing
api
performance
development
engineering

PASS:
BullMQ
Vitest
RLS
Edge Functions
Vue Router
Express Middleware
gRPC Gateway

## RetrievalAssociationFalsePositiveRule

A retrieval_association is invalid if it produces
systematic false positives during corpus evaluation.

Corpus Validation:

Run Aho-Corasick over representative
Vietnamese and English software-engineering
job descriptions.

Reject a retrieval_association if:

false_positive_rate > 20%

or

precision < 80%

for the owning anchor.

## RetrievalAssociationPlatformCoverageRule

Validation corpus must include:

- LinkedIn
- Indeed Vietnam
- VietnamWorks
- ITviec
- TopCV
- CareerViet
- TopDev
- Glints Vietnam
- Company career pages

A retrieval_association may not be accepted
or rejected using a single-platform corpus.

## RetrievalReplacementRule

Rejecting a retrieval_association does not imply reducing
retrieval coverage.

When a retrieval_association fails validation because of:

- genericity
- false-positive rate
- low discriminative score
- low information gain

the generator SHALL attempt to replace it with a more
discriminative retrieval_association from the same anchor
ecosystem.

Deletion is permitted only if no suitable replacement exists.

The objective is to maximize

retrieval precision
AND
retrieval recall

rather than minimizing association count.

## RetrievalAssociationPriorityRule

When multiple candidate retrieval_associations exist,
prefer them in the following order:

1. official technology name
2. official framework ecosystem term
3. runtime terminology
4. protocol terminology
5. deployment terminology
6. architecture terminology
7. vendor ecosystem terminology
8. generic engineering terminology

Lower-priority generic vocabulary shall be replaced by
higher-priority discriminative vocabulary whenever possible.

## LexicalRedundancyRule

Reject retrieval_associations that contribute no additional
lexical retrieval value.

Examples

Reject

Express
ExpressJS
Express.js

Keep

Express.js
Express Router
Express Middleware
Express Session

Each retained association must contribute unique retrieval
evidence for deterministic Aho-Corasick matching.

## CorpusOptimizationRule

Corpus evaluation is authoritative.

When regression testing identifies retrieval_associations
that consistently generate false positives,
future generations shall replace those associations with
higher-discrimination alternatives observed in the corpus.

Corpus evidence takes precedence over ontology-derived
candidate vocabulary.

## RetrievalFeedbackRule

Generation is iterative.

Corpus evaluation metrics shall be used to improve future
retrieval_associations.

Observed metrics include:

- precision
- recall
- false-positive rate
- lexical hit rate
- freeze spots
- dead phrases

Generation should maximize measured retrieval performance
rather than static vocabulary count.

## RetrievalAssociationDiscriminationRule

Every retrieval_association must provide measurable
discriminative power for its owning anchor.

Evidence may include:

- Information Gain
- Mutual Information
- Conditional Probability
- Corpus Precision
- False Positive Rate

A candidate passes if corpus evaluation demonstrates
that it improves anchor identification.

The implementation is free to choose the statistical
measure.

## RetrievalNodePerformanceRule

A relation node is evaluated as a whole.

Validation SHALL optimize the retrieval quality
of the complete node rather than individual
retrieval_associations.

Adding or removing one association is acceptable
only if the aggregate node metrics improve.

Node metrics include:

- Precision
- Recall
- F1
- Mean Hits/JD
- False Positives/JD
- Freeze Spots
- Dead Phrase Count

Node-level metrics take precedence over
individual association metrics.

## MixedLanguageCorpusRule

Corpus evaluation SHALL include:

- English JDs
- Vietnamese JDs
- Mixed Vietnamese-English JDs

Vocabulary that performs well only on one corpus
may not dominate generation.

## TrieEfficiencyRule

A retrieval_association should maximize
expected retrieval utility per indexed token.

Reject vocabulary that:

- never matches
- duplicates another indexed phrase
- contributes negligible recall
- contributes negligible precision

The objective is to maximize

Useful Hits
------------
Trie Entries

## CandidateRankingRule

Candidate retrieval_associations shall be ranked
before selection.

Ranking should consider:

- corpus precision
- corpus recall
- information gain
- lexical uniqueness
- false-positive rate
- ecosystem relevance

Generation shall prefer the highest-ranked
combination rather than evaluating candidates
independently.
